[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded single-control behavioral voltage operating points

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Bounded implementation and verification are recorded in
docs/behavioral-voltage-results.md and evidence/behavioral-voltage.json. The target is
the unchanged original regression/misc/log-functions-1.cir requested OP and its
complete original assertions. Runtime preparation must not replace an arbitrary
voltage-dependent expression by a constant or weaken the native comparison.

Reuse assessment: retain the previously evaluated independent-core decision.
Reuse the existing bounded Rust Expr value/derivative evaluator, native MNA
branch contract and C# generated grammar. Do not introduce another parser or a
legacy runtime dependency. RSpice source pin 29c28a022625fd7cc2c56ead1cce2d3066663074
provides behavioral stamping and expression-domain reference patterns. This is
source inspection; no new RSpice execution is claimed. Its denominator-floor
helper is not evidence that it uses our proposed initialization seed.

Affected path: generated expression lowering -> typed .NET expression
DTO -> Rust request validation -> immutable compiled behavioral branch ->
constitutive residual/Jacobian -> selected CPU provider -> independent value
and conservation audit -> voltage/current reporting. The frontend and typed DTO adapters are implemented. Native and managed builds
and the retained bounded tests pass; this is not general behavioral compatibility.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BEHAVIOR-VOLTAGE-DC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded single-control constitutive voltage relation
STATEMENT: >>>
The DC engine shall support an explicit behavioral voltage relation
Vp-Vn=F(Vcp-Vcn), with branch current oriented P to N. Its typed bounded
expression shall support finite constants, one differential input, addition,
multiplication, division, exponential and natural logarithm, with analytic first
derivatives and explicit source identity. Domain errors, overflow, unknown wire
fields or operations, excessive expression structure and invalid terminals
shall be refused without publishing a partial physical result.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Structural limits: 1024 nodes and depth 64. The wire adapter preserves
the pre-existing Rust tuple-variant Expr API. Seven public runtime tests pass, including 64 Proptest cases with seed
2026111101. The initial two tests failed on the old missing wire variant.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BEHAVIOR-VOLTAGE-SEED-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Linear-constraint seed and unchanged physical equations
STATEMENT: >>>
For default behavioral DC initialization, the engine shall obtain a bounded
linear-constraint seed before domain-sensitive expression evaluation. A seed
may temporarily set behavioral output values to zero solely while establishing
the linear constraints. It shall not be returned as a physical solution.
The actual provider call shall be counted, and final convergence and audit
shall use the full unregularized constitutive equations. A singular seed or
invalid final domain shall be an explicit failure; missing physical data shall
not be replaced by zero to obtain a passing result.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The implementation uses the compiled base MNA matrix through the supplied provider.
Behavioral voltage rows must be excluded from the Newton controller's separate
linear voltage-feasibility classification. Existing nonbehavioral zero-start
behavior is retained. Initialization generally remains a numerical strategy,
not a guarantee of convergence. No positive-floor logarithm is introduced.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BEHAVIOR-VOLTAGE-AUDIT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independent physical audit and explicit qualification boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
Accepted behavioral DC results shall satisfy independent output-constraint,
KCL and power checks. Value reconstruction shall not call the production
derivative evaluator or reuse assembled matrices. AC and transient execution
shall remain explicit unsupported outcomes until independently implemented
and qualified through their public entry points.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verified checks include centered-difference Jacobians, corrupted-state audit
rejection, malformed structures, explicit dynamic refusals and a killed
zero-control-slope mutant. The unchanged logarithm deck agrees on all 14
observables and executes its control assertions. See the behavioral-voltage
checkpoint evidence for measured coverage and remaining qualification limits.
Draft status does not claim general behavioral-source compatibility.
<<<
